<!--meta {"lead": "Forms are where Maya commits: a booking request, a review, her contact details. Every HairPop form is one column, labelled above, validated on submit, and recoverable without retyping.", "description": "Layout, labels, validation timing, the linked error summary, submit and success states.", "covers": "Layout, label placement, validation timing, linked error summary, submitting and success, offline, destructive confirmation"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>A HairPop form is a <a href="../components/card.html">card</a> titled with what it collects, holding one column of <a href="../components/form-field.html">form fields</a>, an optional estimate or note, and one primary <a href="../components/button.html">button</a> that names the outcome ("Send request", "Post review", "Save changes"). The mocks use this shape for booking, care and review, account settings and every auth screen.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>One column.</b> Fields stack in reading order. Two columns appear only for short related pairs at 768px and up (<code>.form-row</code>).</li>
    <li><b>Label above, help below the label, error below the input.</b> Placeholders are hints, never labels.</li>
    <li><b>Validate on submit, then re-validate on input.</b> No errors while Maya is still typing a field for the first time.</li>
    <li><b>Nothing is lost.</b> Errors, offline and failure states keep every value she entered.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="when"><h2><a href="#when">When to use which</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Situation</th><th scope="col">Use</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Collecting several details that create or change something</td><td>Form page in a <code>.form-panel</code> card</td><td>Booking request, account settings</td></tr>
      <tr><td>One or two fields that refine the current screen</td><td><a href="../components/dialog.html">Dialog</a> with a form body</td><td>Filter braiders, request a change</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A final check before something is sent</td><td>Review dialog that repeats the key values</td><td>Review request</td></tr>
      <tr><td>A destructive action</td><td>Confirmation dialog with a danger button; no form fields</td><td>Cancel appointment, sign out</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Editing one value in a list or card</td><td>Button that opens a dialog; never an inline form in the page</td><td>Request a change on the appointment card</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="structure"><h2><a href="#structure">Structure</a></h2>
  <p>Card title, fields, a note that sets expectations, then the action. The primary button is full width on phones and sits at the end of the form from 768px.</p>
  <div class="ds-frame"><div class="ds-frame__body">
    <section class="form-panel card" aria-labelledby="fs-title">
      <h2 id="fs-title">Your details</h2>
      <form class="stack" action="#structure" novalidate>
        <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fs-service">Service</label><input class="input" id="fs-service" name="service" type="text" value="Medium knotless braids"></div>
        <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fs-time">Preferred time</label><span class="field__help" id="fs-time-help">Choose one of the times Nia offers.</span><input class="input" id="fs-time" name="time" type="datetime-local" value="2026-10-24T10:00" aria-describedby="fs-time-help"></div>
        <div class="form-row">
          <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fs-email">Your email</label><input class="input" id="fs-email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" value="maya.chen@example.com"></div>
          <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fs-phone">Phone <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label><input class="input" id="fs-phone" name="phone" type="tel" autocomplete="tel" value="416-555-0148"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fs-hair">Hair details</label><textarea class="textarea" id="fs-hair" name="hair">Shoulder length; bringing my own extensions</textarea></div>
        <p class="text-muted">Estimate: $180–$240 · about 5 hours. Nia confirms the final price and time.</p>
        <div class="form-actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send request</button></div>
      </form>
    </section>
  </div></div>
  <ul>
    <li>Gap between fields: <code>--space-4</code>. Label to input: <code>--space-1</code>. Panel width: <code>--layout-form-max</code> (38rem).</li>
    <li>The card heading uses the h3 role, not the 36px page h2.</li>
    <li>Mark the optional fields, not the required ones, when most fields are required.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <h3>Invalid: summary linked to fields</h3>
  <p>On submit, show a danger <a href="../components/alert.html">alert</a> at the top of the form that names each problem and links to its field, move focus to the summary (it has <code>tabindex="-1"</code>), mark each field <code>aria-invalid="true"</code> and tie its message with <code>aria-describedby</code>.</p>
  <div class="ds-frame"><div class="ds-frame__body">
    <section class="form-panel card" aria-labelledby="fi-title">
      <h2 id="fi-title">Your details</h2>
      <div class="alert alert--danger form-summary" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="fi-sum-title">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div><strong id="fi-sum-title">Check 1 field before sending</strong><ul><li><a href="#fi-time">Preferred time: choose a time Nia offers</a></li></ul></div></div>
      <form class="stack" action="#states" novalidate>
        <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fi-service">Service</label><input class="input" id="fi-service" type="text" value="Medium knotless braids"></div>
        <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fi-time">Preferred time</label><input class="input" id="fi-time" type="datetime-local" value="2026-10-24T08:00" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="fi-time-error"><span class="field__error" id="fi-time-error">Choose a time Nia offers. Her first slot on Sat 24 Oct is 10:00 am.</span></div>
        <div class="form-actions"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="submit">Send request</button></div>
      </form>
    </section>
  </div></div>
  <h3>Submitting, success and offline</h3>
  <div class="ds-example"><div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--start">
    <div class="card stack">
      <p class="overline">Submitting</p>
      <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fb-email">Your email</label><input class="input" id="fb-email" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com"></div>
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" aria-busy="true">Send request</button>
      <p class="inline-status" role="status"><span class="spinner spinner--sm" aria-hidden="true"></span>Sending your request to Nia…</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card"><section class="empty empty--compact"><div class="empty__icon" aria-hidden="true">{{icon:check}}</div><h2 class="empty__title">Request sent to Nia</h2><p class="empty__text">This is a request, not a confirmed appointment. Nia will reply with the final time and price.</p><div class="empty__actions"><a class="btn btn--primary" href="../../mocks/pages/appointment-detail/default.html">View request</a></div></section></div>
    <div class="card stack">
      <div class="alert alert--warning">{{icon:wifi-off}}<div><strong>You’re offline.</strong> Your details stay here. Connect before sending.</div></div>
      <div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="fo-email">Your email</label><input class="input" id="fo-email" type="email" value="maya.chen@example.com"></div>
      <button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Send request</button>
    </div>
  </div><div class="ds-example__caption"><span>Busy keeps the label and focus; success replaces the form with a next step; offline keeps the button enabled and explains on activation.</span></div></div>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Submitting</b>: only the pressed button gets <code>aria-busy="true"</code>; fields stay editable and nothing is disabled. Progress text goes to a <code>role="status"</code> region.</li>
    <li><b>Failed</b> (server error): keep the form, add a danger alert above it ("We couldn’t send your request. Your details are still here. Try again."), and keep focus on the button.</li>
    <li><b>Success</b>: replace the form with a success <a href="../components/empty-state.html">empty state</a> that states what happens next and links to it. Forms that stay on screen (account settings) use a success toast instead.</li>
    <li><b>Destructive confirmation</b>: never a form. See <a href="dialogs-and-overlays.html">dialogs and overlays</a>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Under 768px: one column, the panel fills the container, the primary button is full width and first in <code>.form-actions</code>.</li>
    <li>From 768px: <code>.form-row</code> pairs short related fields (email and phone, city and postal code); the primary returns to its natural width at the end.</li>
    <li>Inputs stay 40px tall with 16px text at every width, which also stops iOS from zooming on focus.</li>
    <li>The summary is not sticky; it scrolls into view because it receives focus.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every input has a visible <code>&lt;label for&gt;</code>. Help and error text are siblings of the input, linked with <code>aria-describedby</code>; never inside the <code>&lt;label&gt;</code>, which would read the error as part of the name.</li>
    <li><code>novalidate</code> on the form; validation messages are ours, written to name the fix (3.3.1, 3.3.3).</li>
    <li>On a failed submit, focus moves to the summary (programmatically, not with <code>autofocus</code>), and each summary link moves focus to its field.</li>
    <li><code>autocomplete</code> on name, email, phone and password fields (1.3.5); paste and password managers are always allowed (3.3.8).</li>
    <li>Information Maya already gave (service, time chosen on Nia’s profile) is pre-filled (3.3.7).</li>
    <li>Busy and offline states never disable the submit button, so it stays focusable and explains itself.</li>
  </ul>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Error text on card|--color-danger-fg|--color-bg-surface|4.5}}
    {{pair:Invalid input edge|--color-danger-solid|--color-bg-surface|3}}
    {{pair:Input edge|--color-border-strong|--color-bg-surface|3}}
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Card titles say what is collected: "Your details", "Your review", "Contact details".</li>
    <li>Labels are nouns in sentence case: "Preferred time", "Your email". Questions only when the answer is a choice: "How did it go?"</li>
    <li>Error formula: <b>what to do + why or an example</b>. "Enter an email address like name@example.com." Not "Invalid input".</li>
    <li>The summary title counts the problems: "Check 1 field before sending", "Check 2 fields before saving".</li>
    <li>Set expectations beside the button when the outcome is not final: "Nia confirms the final price and time."</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="field"><label class="field__label" for="dd-email-a">Email</label><input class="input" id="dd-email-a" type="email" value="maya.chen@" aria-invalid="true" aria-describedby="dd-email-a-err"><span class="field__error" id="dd-email-a-err">Enter an email address like name@example.com.</span></div></div><figcaption>Error text beside the input, linked with <code>aria-describedby</code>, saying how to fix it.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><div class="alert alert--danger form-summary">{{icon:alert-circle}}<div><strong>Check the highlighted field</strong><p>Correct the information below and try again.</p></div></div></div><figcaption>A summary that names no field and links nowhere, focused with <code>autofocus</code> (as the mocks’ invalid states do).</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" aria-busy="true">Post review</button></div><figcaption>While sending, the button keeps its label and focus and sets <code>aria-busy</code>.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button" disabled>Working…</button></div><figcaption>Disabling the button and relabelling it "Working…" drops focus and hides what is happening.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/default|form panel, estimate note}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/invalid|error summary and field error}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/submitting|busy submit}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/success|success replaces the form}}
    {{mock:pages/booking-request/offline|offline banner above the form}}
    {{mock:pages/account-settings/invalid|email error copy}}
    {{mock:pages/care-and-review/invalid|rating error copy}}
    {{mock:dialogs/filter-braiders/invalid|form in a dialog}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed: the error summary named no field, linked nowhere and used <code>autofocus</code> (now lists linked errors and receives focus on submit); field errors were rendered inside the <code>&lt;label&gt;</code> (now a sibling linked with <code>aria-describedby</code>); busy buttons were disabled and relabelled "Working…" (now <code>aria-busy</code> only); offline forms disabled the button (now enabled, with the offline banner explaining).</p>
</section>
